1
00:00:00,570 --> 00:00:03,279
Have I really fallen for him?

2
00:00:03,280 --> 00:00:04,220
Fallen for So-chan...

3
00:00:04,221 --> 00:00:06,559
I guess you don't need
tutoring anymore, right?

4
00:00:06,560 --> 00:00:08,799
I'm really happy when I'm with Natsuki.

5
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:12,699
I feel so lucky to have
met someone like him.

6
00:00:12,700 --> 00:00:16,279
You mean you want to
try and understand him?

7
00:00:16,280 --> 00:00:18,330
Yeah, something like that.

8
00:00:25,840 --> 00:00:28,299
(Well done! That's great!)

9
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:31,320
So-chan is leaving.

10
00:00:32,510 --> 00:00:34,279
(A few hours ago)

11
00:00:34,280 --> 00:00:35,519
The UK?

12
00:00:35,520 --> 00:00:36,520
Yeah.

13
00:00:37,130 --> 00:00:38,620
I've decided to study abroad.

14
00:00:39,480 --> 00:00:40,240
What?

15
00:00:40,241 --> 00:00:43,040
I originally applied for next year.

16
00:00:44,250 --> 00:00:45,250
Huh?

17
00:00:45,320 --> 00:00:47,099
But they said a spot
opened up in September.

18
00:00:47,100 --> 00:00:48,940
And asked if I wanted to go.

19
00:00:50,520 --> 00:00:54,439
Is that to learn how to build bridges?

20
00:00:54,440 --> 00:00:55,120
Yeah.

21
00:00:55,400 --> 00:00:59,899
I'll first study at a university where a
famous bridge mechanics scholar teaches.

22
00:00:59,900 --> 00:01:02,840
Then I'll gain on-site
experience through an internship.

23
00:01:04,910 --> 00:01:06,200
For how long?

24
00:01:06,890 --> 00:01:07,890
Two years.

25
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:12,750
I see.

26
00:01:18,300 --> 00:01:19,580
That's amazing.

27
00:01:20,200 --> 00:01:21,260
Congratulations.

28
00:01:23,690 --> 00:01:24,690
Thanks.

29
00:01:28,110 --> 00:01:29,180
Mmm...

30
00:01:29,680 --> 00:01:31,230
It's delicious.

31
00:01:31,880 --> 00:01:33,159
Ryo, this is on the house.

32
00:01:33,160 --> 00:01:34,269
Oh, really?

33
00:01:34,270 --> 00:01:35,270
Awesome.

34
00:01:36,220 --> 00:01:39,000
If only I could ship this to you in the UK.

35
00:01:39,850 --> 00:01:40,440
Huh?

36
00:01:40,780 --> 00:01:42,379
Sota-san is going to the UK?

37
00:01:42,380 --> 00:01:42,920
Yeah.

38
00:01:42,921 --> 00:01:44,429
Seriously?

39
00:01:44,430 --> 00:01:45,840
Yeah.

40
00:01:46,460 --> 00:01:49,020
Natsuki is definitely going to be lonely.

41
00:01:51,470 --> 00:01:52,470
Welcome.

42
00:01:53,310 --> 00:01:54,480
Natsuki.

43
00:01:55,240 --> 00:01:56,240
Oh.

44
00:01:56,590 --> 00:01:57,590
Ah.

45
00:01:57,820 --> 00:01:59,959
Here, almond tofu, on the house.

46
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:00,650
Okay, almond tofu.

47
00:02:00,651 --> 00:02:02,240
Thanks.

48
00:02:03,390 --> 00:02:04,569
Oh...

49
00:02:04,570 --> 00:02:05,769
So...

50
00:02:05,770 --> 00:02:08,679
Are you going to tutor him
in math online from the UK?

51
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:09,680
Yeah.

52
00:02:10,190 --> 00:02:12,239
It's fine, don't worry about me.

53
00:02:12,240 --> 00:02:13,319
It does matter.

54
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:14,060
Exactly.

55
00:02:14,061 --> 00:02:16,039
Natsuki, if you keep
slacking off like this...

56
00:02:16,040 --> 00:02:17,369
I'm going to surpass you.

57
00:02:17,370 --> 00:02:18,759
That's right.

58
00:02:18,760 --> 00:02:20,429
I heard Ryo is going to cram school now.

59
00:02:20,430 --> 00:02:20,840
Yeah.

60
00:02:20,841 --> 00:02:22,009
Oh, really?

61
00:02:22,010 --> 00:02:23,999
He saw Natsuki's grades improving...

62
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:25,579
And thought he'd be in trouble
if he didn't do something, right?

63
00:02:25,580 --> 00:02:27,320
But if I actually get serious...

64
00:02:27,690 --> 00:02:29,290
Beating Natsuki will be a piece of cake.

65
00:02:30,010 --> 00:02:31,560
Did you hear that, Na-chan?

66
00:02:32,680 --> 00:02:33,560
Ah.

67
00:02:33,561 --> 00:02:35,309
Like I'd ever lose to Ryo.

68
00:02:35,310 --> 00:02:36,240
Wait, were you even listening?

69
00:02:36,241 --> 00:02:37,900
Did you hear what he just said?

70
00:02:40,320 --> 00:02:41,340
Na-chan.

71
00:02:42,280 --> 00:02:44,680
Is there something you want to say?

72
00:02:45,370 --> 00:02:47,209
Huh? Why do you ask?

73
00:02:47,210 --> 00:02:48,210
Nothing at all.

74
00:02:48,640 --> 00:02:50,090
Are you sure?

75
00:02:50,380 --> 00:02:50,960
Yeah.

76
00:02:50,960 --> 00:02:51,960
I just feel like...

77
00:02:52,620 --> 00:02:55,210
You're acting a bit different today.

78
00:02:56,190 --> 00:02:57,190
Huh?

79
00:02:58,380 --> 00:02:59,850
No, you're just overthinking it.

80
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:02,729
Well then, I'll see you
for tutoring tomorrow.

81
00:03:02,730 --> 00:03:03,730
Yeah.

82
00:03:04,250 --> 00:03:05,150
See you tomorrow.

83
00:03:05,150 --> 00:03:06,150
Yeah.

84
00:03:26,590 --> 00:03:28,990
"Your Summer, My Storm"
(Episode 10)

85
00:03:30,860 --> 00:03:31,860
Sigh...

86
00:03:37,080 --> 00:03:38,699
This is bad...

87
00:03:38,700 --> 00:03:42,920
The more I try to act normal,
the more awkward it gets.

88
00:03:44,030 --> 00:03:45,900
Let's go, Jack.

89
00:03:48,490 --> 00:03:49,819
So cute!

90
00:03:49,820 --> 00:03:50,720
Ah.

91
00:03:50,720 --> 00:03:51,480
Excuse me.

92
00:03:51,481 --> 00:03:53,279
He's super cute.

93
00:03:53,280 --> 00:03:54,190
Can I pet him?

94
00:03:54,190 --> 00:03:55,190
Sure.

95
00:03:56,120 --> 00:03:57,390
So cute.

96
00:03:57,680 --> 00:03:59,279
Second only to my dog.

97
00:03:59,280 --> 00:04:00,759
Good for you, Jack.

98
00:04:00,760 --> 00:04:02,119
His name is Jack?

99
00:04:02,120 --> 00:04:02,670
Yes.

100
00:04:02,670 --> 00:04:03,320
I see.

101
00:04:03,321 --> 00:04:05,209
I have a Samoyed at home, too.

102
00:04:05,210 --> 00:04:06,649
His name is Rock.

103
00:04:06,650 --> 00:04:07,360
Rock?

104
00:04:07,360 --> 00:04:08,190
Yes.

105
00:04:08,191 --> 00:04:09,850
That's a cool name.

106
00:04:10,240 --> 00:04:11,240
Thanks.

107
00:04:11,400 --> 00:04:12,799
He's very well-behaved.

108
00:04:12,800 --> 00:04:15,359
Even people who are
scared of dogs like him.

109
00:04:15,360 --> 00:04:18,160
Rock's feelings must have
gotten through to them.

110
00:04:20,440 --> 00:04:21,440
Yes.

111
00:04:22,200 --> 00:04:23,200
Oh.

112
00:04:23,820 --> 00:04:24,800
It's nothing.

113
00:04:24,801 --> 00:04:26,200
Please don't mind me.

114
00:04:31,390 --> 00:04:32,390
Here.

115
00:04:33,530 --> 00:04:36,280
When you want to cry, just let it out.

116
00:04:44,430 --> 00:04:46,030
Jack says so, too.

117
00:04:46,480 --> 00:04:47,740
Jack.

118
00:05:00,090 --> 00:05:01,900
We can't see the stars today.

119
00:05:07,980 --> 00:05:09,950
We can't see the stars today.

120
00:05:10,670 --> 00:05:11,670
Huh?

121
00:05:15,690 --> 00:05:19,100
(I was just looking at the sky, too.)

122
00:05:22,130 --> 00:05:24,379
(Kobayakawa Sota)
(ID: SOTA0830)

123
00:05:24,380 --> 00:05:25,210
Wait.

124
00:05:25,211 --> 00:05:27,150
Could this be...

125
00:05:27,850 --> 00:05:29,869
Rock, I'm home.

126
00:05:29,870 --> 00:05:31,049
- Sis.
- Oh.

127
00:05:31,050 --> 00:05:33,399
Do you know when So-chan's birthday is?

128
00:05:33,400 --> 00:05:34,680
His birthday?

129
00:05:36,430 --> 00:05:38,999
I think it's August 30th.

130
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,589
Isn't that coming up soon?

131
00:05:40,590 --> 00:05:41,470
I see.

132
00:05:41,470 --> 00:05:42,060
Oh.

133
00:05:42,061 --> 00:05:43,420
Should we throw a birthday party?

134
00:05:43,790 --> 00:05:44,790
Ah.

135
00:05:44,880 --> 00:05:47,280
But you guys probably want
to celebrate just the two of you.

136
00:05:47,310 --> 00:05:48,310
Not really...

137
00:05:50,700 --> 00:05:52,359
Don't tell me...

138
00:05:52,360 --> 00:05:54,970
You're upset because Sota is leaving...

139
00:05:55,320 --> 00:05:56,599
And you're throwing a tantrum?

140
00:05:56,600 --> 00:05:58,539
N-No, it's not like that.

141
00:05:58,540 --> 00:06:02,219
But you can't bring yourself to
say "Don't go" or "I'll miss you."

142
00:06:02,220 --> 00:06:04,300
So you're pretending like
everything is fine, right?

143
00:06:04,510 --> 00:06:07,789
Because it's embarrassing, isn't it?

144
00:06:07,790 --> 00:06:09,960
What? Why are you saying this now?

145
00:06:10,480 --> 00:06:11,760
What do you mean, "now"?

146
00:06:12,560 --> 00:06:16,799
When you're in love, it's normal to
get happy or sad over little things.

147
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:19,580
Other people might even find it funny.

148
00:06:20,410 --> 00:06:24,170
But the power of love makes
you do it without feeling ashamed.

149
00:06:25,560 --> 00:06:27,160
Being honest is the best policy.

150
00:06:27,870 --> 00:06:29,340
Isn't that right, Rock?

151
00:06:40,730 --> 00:06:41,730
Ah.

152
00:06:45,230 --> 00:06:47,320
Let me cancel tomorrow's lesson.

153
00:06:47,640 --> 00:06:48,640
Huh?

154
00:06:56,510 --> 00:06:58,509
Sorry, let me cancel today's lesson.

155
00:06:58,510 --> 00:06:59,510
Huh?

156
00:07:03,800 --> 00:07:04,999
I'm really sorry.

157
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:06,250
I have to cancel today, too.

158
00:07:06,600 --> 00:07:07,660
Why?

159
00:07:11,340 --> 00:07:12,840
Sorry, tomorrow as well.

160
00:07:14,300 --> 00:07:16,270
He's avoiding me...

161
00:07:17,620 --> 00:07:19,920
(August 30th)

162
00:07:36,170 --> 00:07:38,900
(It's fine if we don't have
a lesson, but can we meet?) [Left on read]

163
00:07:49,130 --> 00:07:50,300
Rio?

164
00:07:54,380 --> 00:07:55,530
Hello.

165
00:07:55,800 --> 00:07:56,750
Sota?

166
00:07:56,751 --> 00:07:57,760
Get over here quickly.

167
00:07:58,190 --> 00:07:59,630
Natsuki is done for.

168
00:07:59,960 --> 00:08:00,960
What?

169
00:08:11,270 --> 00:08:12,859
Sota, hurry.

170
00:08:12,860 --> 00:08:14,180
Is Na-chan okay?

171
00:08:17,400 --> 00:08:18,540
Welcome.

172
00:08:19,380 --> 00:08:20,490
Welcome.

173
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:22,660
Huh? Na-chan?

174
00:08:23,000 --> 00:08:24,040
Are you okay?

175
00:08:24,360 --> 00:08:25,360
Yeah.

176
00:08:25,500 --> 00:08:28,460
I only said Natsuki was done for, right?

177
00:08:28,980 --> 00:08:29,980
Huh?

178
00:08:31,430 --> 00:08:32,430
Ah.

179
00:08:33,450 --> 00:08:37,420
Yeah, Natsuki is swamped.

180
00:08:37,880 --> 00:08:40,650
I made everything here except the bread.

181
00:08:41,240 --> 00:08:42,379
Seriously?

182
00:08:42,380 --> 00:08:44,620
It's all Sota's favorite food, right?

183
00:08:45,240 --> 00:08:46,240
Yeah.

184
00:08:47,103 --> 00:08:49,002
This was really hard.

185
00:08:49,030 --> 00:08:51,669
Na-chan, that's not how you hold it.

186
00:08:51,670 --> 00:08:52,230
Huh?

187
00:08:52,231 --> 00:08:53,459
- Hey, Na-chan.
- Yes.

188
00:08:53,460 --> 00:08:54,979
Keep an eye on the pot, too.

189
00:08:54,980 --> 00:08:56,470
Ah, sorry.

190
00:08:57,540 --> 00:08:59,530
- Hot!
- That's really hot.

191
00:08:59,960 --> 00:09:00,740
This tastes awful.

192
00:09:00,740 --> 00:09:01,540
No way.

193
00:09:01,540 --> 00:09:02,360
Yeah.

194
00:09:02,361 --> 00:09:03,500
Here.

195
00:09:06,860 --> 00:09:07,899
It tastes awful.

196
00:09:07,900 --> 00:09:13,690
I prepped all the ingredients for you.
How could you mess it up this badly?

197
00:09:13,940 --> 00:09:14,980
Sorry.

198
00:09:15,340 --> 00:09:16,170
Natsuki.

199
00:09:16,170 --> 00:09:16,660
Yes.

200
00:09:16,661 --> 00:09:19,129
Didn't I tell you to cut
it into bite-sized pieces?

201
00:09:19,130 --> 00:09:19,700
I'm sorry.

202
00:09:19,701 --> 00:09:22,299
If apologies worked, we wouldn't need cops.

203
00:09:22,300 --> 00:09:22,900
Yes.

204
00:09:22,901 --> 00:09:25,179
Isn't Uncle acting a
bit different from usual?

205
00:09:25,180 --> 00:09:26,919
He gets like this whenever
it comes to cooking.

206
00:09:26,920 --> 00:09:27,610
I see.

207
00:09:27,611 --> 00:09:28,859
That's wrong.

208
00:09:28,860 --> 00:09:30,859
How many times do I have to tell you?

209
00:09:30,860 --> 00:09:31,420
I'm sorry.

210
00:09:31,421 --> 00:09:33,719
I feel sorry for the chicken
that ended up in your hands.

211
00:09:33,720 --> 00:09:34,810
Huh?

212
00:09:38,200 --> 00:09:39,200
Why?

213
00:09:39,930 --> 00:09:40,870
What do you mean, why?

214
00:09:40,871 --> 00:09:42,520
Isn't today your birthday?

215
00:09:43,270 --> 00:09:43,930
Huh?

216
00:09:43,931 --> 00:09:47,750
Happy birthday!

217
00:09:48,250 --> 00:09:49,100
Ah.

218
00:09:49,101 --> 00:09:50,939
I completely forgot.

219
00:09:50,940 --> 00:09:51,959
What?

220
00:09:51,960 --> 00:09:52,860
Really?

221
00:09:52,860 --> 00:09:53,860
Yeah.

222
00:09:53,940 --> 00:09:54,520
Ah.

223
00:09:54,950 --> 00:09:57,059
Is that why you canceled
at the last minute?

224
00:09:57,060 --> 00:09:57,740
Yeah.

225
00:09:58,060 --> 00:10:00,330
Ah, but I still did my studying, though.

226
00:10:01,000 --> 00:10:04,039
I originally suggested
throwing a big party.

227
00:10:04,040 --> 00:10:07,349
But Natsuki said he wanted a
cozy, family-style birthday party.

228
00:10:07,350 --> 00:10:09,369
He also said Sota-san had never
celebrated his birthday like this.

229
00:10:09,370 --> 00:10:12,740
So this would definitely
make you the happiest.

230
00:10:13,430 --> 00:10:15,939
I didn't really want to join at first.

231
00:10:15,940 --> 00:10:16,940
Yeah.

232
00:10:17,060 --> 00:10:20,389
After all, Sota really loves our family.

233
00:10:20,390 --> 00:10:22,169
Of course, we all had to be here.

234
00:10:22,170 --> 00:10:23,750
Right?

235
00:10:24,650 --> 00:10:25,650
Yes.

236
00:10:26,500 --> 00:10:27,500
Thank you.

237
00:10:28,220 --> 00:10:28,970
Yeah.

238
00:10:28,971 --> 00:10:30,299
Alright, come sit down.

239
00:10:30,300 --> 00:10:31,510
(Rock)
- Let's eat. - Okay.

240
00:10:32,500 --> 00:10:33,579
- Mmm.
- Not bad.

241
00:10:33,580 --> 00:10:34,759
The yurinchi is so good!

242
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:35,690
Really?

243
00:10:35,691 --> 00:10:38,390
It's not as good as Uncle's,
but it's still delicious.

244
00:10:38,900 --> 00:10:40,199
It's super tasty.

245
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:41,829
- That's great.
- Okay.

246
00:10:41,830 --> 00:10:43,449
- Eat up.
- Eat as much as you want.

247
00:10:43,450 --> 00:10:44,809
- Try this.
- This one too.

248
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:46,310
How does it taste?

249
00:10:46,760 --> 00:10:48,729
No rush, take your time.

250
00:10:48,730 --> 00:10:49,879
(Happy Birthday, So-chan)
Okay.

251
00:10:49,880 --> 00:10:50,899
Careful.

252
00:10:50,900 --> 00:10:51,850
Ready?

253
00:10:51,851 --> 00:10:53,559
Wow, that's amazing.

254
00:10:53,560 --> 00:10:54,560
Here.

255
00:10:54,900 --> 00:10:55,939
Um...

256
00:10:55,940 --> 00:10:58,040
If you don't mind, this is for you.

257
00:10:58,527 --> 00:11:00,066
It's an LED flashlight.

258
00:11:00,090 --> 00:11:00,740
Huh?

259
00:11:00,741 --> 00:11:02,149
Oh, honestly.

260
00:11:02,150 --> 00:11:03,979
Isn't that your old one?

261
00:11:03,980 --> 00:11:06,219
Idiot, why would I do that?

262
00:11:06,220 --> 00:11:08,199
I bought a new one, okay?

263
00:11:08,200 --> 00:11:09,719
Oh, is that so?

264
00:11:09,720 --> 00:11:11,060
Of course.

265
00:11:11,480 --> 00:11:13,079
This is actually pretty useful.

266
00:11:13,080 --> 00:11:13,990
Thank you, Uncle.

267
00:11:13,991 --> 00:11:15,129
I'll gladly accept it.

268
00:11:15,130 --> 00:11:16,469
And here,

269
00:11:16,470 --> 00:11:18,139
this is from me.

270
00:11:18,140 --> 00:11:20,069
Wow, I'm so happy.

271
00:11:20,070 --> 00:11:21,189
Thank you, Auntie.

272
00:11:21,190 --> 00:11:24,219
If you're taking it with you, you
can't bring it in your carry-on.

273
00:11:24,220 --> 00:11:25,190
Be careful with that.

274
00:11:25,191 --> 00:11:26,220
Got it.

275
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,550
And then, here.

276
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:30,599
This is from me.

277
00:11:30,600 --> 00:11:31,530
(To So-chan)

278
00:11:31,530 --> 00:11:32,530
Huh?

279
00:11:37,160 --> 00:11:38,200
What is this...?

280
00:11:38,710 --> 00:11:39,400
Open it and see.

281
00:11:39,700 --> 00:11:40,700
Okay.

282
00:11:41,626 --> 00:11:44,252
[Birthday emssages and
messages of encouragement]

283
00:11:45,270 --> 00:11:47,020
Wow, this is amazing.

284
00:11:47,420 --> 00:11:49,189
This wasn't easy to make, you know.

285
00:11:49,190 --> 00:11:50,629
- Hey!
- Yay!

286
00:11:50,630 --> 00:11:51,639
So-chan.

287
00:11:51,640 --> 00:11:53,559
- Happy birthday!
- Yay!

288
00:11:53,560 --> 00:11:55,700
Ah, this isn't a video.

289
00:11:56,550 --> 00:11:58,329
- Oh, come on.
- You should've said so!

290
00:11:58,330 --> 00:11:59,349
- It's a photo.
- Okay.

291
00:11:59,350 --> 00:12:00,060
I'm taking it.

292
00:12:00,061 --> 00:12:01,239
Yay!

293
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:02,600
(Enjoy every day!)
(Do your best!)

294
00:12:04,900 --> 00:12:05,480
(Riku)

295
00:12:05,481 --> 00:12:07,270
Come on, smile.

296
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:08,649
Riku.

297
00:12:08,650 --> 00:12:11,289
Let's strike a rock 'n' roll pose.

298
00:12:11,290 --> 00:12:12,290
Woof!

299
00:12:12,500 --> 00:12:14,329
No, I didn't mean Rock the dog.

300
00:12:14,330 --> 00:12:15,330
(Thank you, Riku)

301
00:12:17,130 --> 00:12:18,439
(Eat Yurinchi over there too)
Wait, Dad, you're way too stiff.

302
00:12:18,440 --> 00:12:19,539
It's gonna steal my soul.

303
00:12:19,540 --> 00:12:20,999
- Alright, I'm taking it anyway.
- Huh?

304
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:22,680
Come on, smile.

305
00:12:23,700 --> 00:12:25,060
(Keep moving forward)
My eyes...

306
00:12:27,120 --> 00:12:28,070
(Rio-san is mine)
(Please teach me math too)

307
00:12:28,071 --> 00:12:29,579
These turned out great.

308
00:12:29,580 --> 00:12:31,559
To Sota-san.

309
00:12:31,560 --> 00:12:33,769
Ryo, you misspelled Sota-san's name.

310
00:12:33,770 --> 00:12:34,390
Huh?
(To Sotta-san)

311
00:12:34,390 --> 00:12:35,340
(To Sotta-san)
- Seriously? - Yeah.

312
00:12:35,341 --> 00:12:38,061
You're supposed to be taking
entrance exams, aren't you embarrassed?

313
00:12:38,230 --> 00:12:39,832
Um, Kazu-kun, you too.

314
00:12:39,856 --> 00:12:41,576
(To Soda-san, when
you go to the UK...) Huh?

315
00:12:42,460 --> 00:12:44,070
Kazu-kun.

316
00:12:47,400 --> 00:12:49,509
(Let's drink together next time)
- Come closer. - No, don't get so close.

317
00:12:49,510 --> 00:12:51,529
Alright, back off.

318
00:12:51,530 --> 00:12:52,579
Okay, I'm taking it.

319
00:12:52,580 --> 00:12:54,069
Smile.

320
00:12:54,070 --> 00:12:56,150
Good boy, good boy.

321
00:12:56,420 --> 00:12:58,390
But really, this is pretty fun.

322
00:12:59,760 --> 00:13:01,960
(You'll always be my rival)
(I'll win next time, Uesugi)

323
00:13:04,600 --> 00:13:07,049
(Takemiya Towako)
(Sota-san, let's eat together again)

324
00:13:07,050 --> 00:13:09,929
I helped take the photos of
Uesugi and the university folks.

325
00:13:09,930 --> 00:13:11,769
Yeah, you did.

326
00:13:11,770 --> 00:13:14,410
(Natsuki, I'll wait for you)
Aren't you lacking a bit of gratitude?

327
00:13:17,820 --> 00:13:19,300
I'm super happy.

328
00:13:20,620 --> 00:13:21,880
Thank you.

329
00:13:25,050 --> 00:13:27,110
And thank you too, Rock.

330
00:13:28,950 --> 00:13:29,560
Here.

331
00:13:29,560 --> 00:13:30,440
You two stand together.

332
00:13:30,441 --> 00:13:31,769
No, it's fine.

333
00:13:31,770 --> 00:13:33,209
- What's the big deal?
- Ah.

334
00:13:33,210 --> 00:13:35,529
It's okay, we'll turn around.

335
00:13:35,530 --> 00:13:37,609
Huh? Why?

336
00:13:37,610 --> 00:13:39,320
Hurry, now's your chance.

337
00:13:39,610 --> 00:13:40,610
Rock.

338
00:13:41,500 --> 00:13:42,170
Go over there.

339
00:13:42,171 --> 00:13:43,509
(Happy Birthday)
Looks great.

340
00:13:43,510 --> 00:13:45,300
Come on, smile.

341
00:13:46,810 --> 00:13:48,999
(Natsuki, Sota)
Not bad, right?

342
00:13:49,000 --> 00:13:50,300
Are you putting this one in too?

343
00:13:51,930 --> 00:13:53,910
I'm really happy.

344
00:13:55,000 --> 00:13:56,659
I'm glad you like it.

345
00:13:56,660 --> 00:13:57,660
Yeah.

346
00:14:06,650 --> 00:14:07,750
What's wrong?

347
00:14:08,950 --> 00:14:09,950
Uh...

348
00:14:10,300 --> 00:14:11,300
How should I put it...

349
00:14:12,540 --> 00:14:14,010
I feel a bit lonely...?

350
00:14:15,720 --> 00:14:16,720
Huh?

351
00:14:17,910 --> 00:14:19,559
I originally thought
two years would fly by.

352
00:14:19,560 --> 00:14:22,620
And with video calls, it wouldn't
feel like we're that far apart.

353
00:14:23,420 --> 00:14:24,420
But...

354
00:14:24,940 --> 00:14:29,720
Now it's finally hitting me that
we're really going to be so far away.

355
00:14:32,260 --> 00:14:35,640
When fun things end, you
always feel a bit lonely, right?

356
00:14:36,150 --> 00:14:37,370
Like after a field trip,

357
00:14:38,580 --> 00:14:40,020
or a sports day.

358
00:14:40,780 --> 00:14:42,710
So that's what it is...

359
00:14:43,560 --> 00:14:45,210
Huh? Isn't it?

360
00:14:45,460 --> 00:14:46,460
No.

361
00:14:46,760 --> 00:14:51,420
I've actually never
really felt lonely before.

362
00:14:52,390 --> 00:14:53,909
Huh? Seriously?

363
00:14:53,910 --> 00:14:54,910
Yeah, really.

364
00:14:55,370 --> 00:14:59,020
I feel like this might be the
first time I've ever felt this way.

365
00:14:59,540 --> 00:15:01,500
Oh, I see.

366
00:15:02,520 --> 00:15:03,720
For me,

367
00:15:04,020 --> 00:15:07,560
just not seeing Rock for a little
while makes me so lonely I want to cry.

368
00:15:10,440 --> 00:15:12,200
At times like this,

369
00:15:12,950 --> 00:15:13,950
what do you do?

370
00:15:14,970 --> 00:15:16,580
Hmm...

371
00:15:17,750 --> 00:15:21,640
I just imagine the next time we'll meet.

372
00:15:24,170 --> 00:15:25,370
I see.

373
00:15:26,040 --> 00:15:27,140
Yeah.

374
00:15:38,100 --> 00:15:39,569
Do you want to study at my place later?

375
00:15:39,570 --> 00:15:40,500
Sure.

376
00:15:40,501 --> 00:15:42,209
But I want to eat sesame dumplings.

377
00:15:42,210 --> 00:15:43,750
- Hmm... No.
- Oh.

378
00:15:44,560 --> 00:15:45,560
Huh?

379
00:15:46,210 --> 00:15:47,700
Sota-san...?

380
00:15:47,960 --> 00:15:48,960
Yeah.

381
00:15:49,190 --> 00:15:50,190
Huh?

382
00:15:55,920 --> 00:15:56,770
Yeah.

383
00:15:56,771 --> 00:15:59,079
Is Sota-san leaving?

384
00:15:59,080 --> 00:16:00,080
Yeah.

385
00:16:00,230 --> 00:16:01,679
I heard it's next week, right?

386
00:16:01,680 --> 00:16:02,480
Wow.

387
00:16:02,481 --> 00:16:03,599
Welcome, Rio-san.

388
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:04,260
Hello, you two.

389
00:16:04,260 --> 00:16:05,090
Good work today.

390
00:16:05,090 --> 00:16:05,750
By the way,

391
00:16:05,751 --> 00:16:08,130
is Sota-san leaving for the UK today?

392
00:16:08,470 --> 00:16:09,509
No.

393
00:16:09,510 --> 00:16:10,120
Huh?

394
00:16:10,390 --> 00:16:13,269
But we just saw him walking
by with a huge suitcase.

395
00:16:13,270 --> 00:16:14,270
What?

396
00:16:18,690 --> 00:16:20,620
(Incoming Call: Rio)

397
00:16:22,790 --> 00:16:23,510
Hello?

398
00:16:23,510 --> 00:16:24,120
Natsuki.

399
00:16:24,121 --> 00:16:25,250
Sota is leaving.

400
00:16:25,960 --> 00:16:26,370
What?

401
00:16:26,371 --> 00:16:29,011
Kazu-kun and the others said
they saw him leave with his suitcase.

402
00:16:29,120 --> 00:16:29,700
What?

403
00:16:29,701 --> 00:16:31,240
He headed toward the bus station.

404
00:16:34,000 --> 00:16:35,600
Go after him, Natsuki!

405
00:16:49,960 --> 00:16:51,030
So-chan!

406
00:16:52,370 --> 00:16:53,460
Why?

407
00:17:17,080 --> 00:17:18,719
So-chan!

408
00:17:18,720 --> 00:17:19,720
Huh?

409
00:17:19,960 --> 00:17:21,170
So-chan!

410
00:17:24,390 --> 00:17:25,730
So-chan!

411
00:17:26,950 --> 00:17:28,240
Na-chan...?

412
00:17:38,550 --> 00:17:39,600
Why...

413
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:42,960
Why did you leave without saying anything?

414
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:47,400
Didn't you say you were leaving next week?

415
00:17:48,500 --> 00:17:49,500
Ah.

416
00:17:50,280 --> 00:17:52,480
I am going to the UK next week, yeah.

417
00:17:53,350 --> 00:17:54,350
I just wanted to...

418
00:17:54,870 --> 00:17:56,230
visit my hometown first.

419
00:17:56,920 --> 00:17:57,600
Huh?

420
00:17:57,601 --> 00:17:59,320
Oh, I see.

421
00:17:59,840 --> 00:18:00,840
Yeah.

422
00:18:01,430 --> 00:18:02,430
But...

423
00:18:03,040 --> 00:18:06,360
I was also thinking about not coming back
and heading straight to the UK from there.

424
00:18:06,870 --> 00:18:08,870
So you did want to leave
without saying anything!

425
00:18:10,710 --> 00:18:11,840
Why?

426
00:18:15,140 --> 00:18:16,180
So-chan.

427
00:18:18,040 --> 00:18:19,040
Because...

428
00:18:19,730 --> 00:18:21,440
Because what?

429
00:18:27,330 --> 00:18:28,330
Huh?

430
00:18:28,480 --> 00:18:30,180
That's why I didn't want to see you...

431
00:18:33,400 --> 00:18:35,280
Because I was afraid that
the moment I saw you,

432
00:18:36,840 --> 00:18:38,320
I'd start crying.

433
00:18:39,240 --> 00:18:42,019
Whether I'm studying, cooking...

434
00:18:42,020 --> 00:18:44,820
taking a shower, or riding the train.

435
00:18:47,540 --> 00:18:49,330
Whenever I think of you,

436
00:18:51,010 --> 00:18:52,320
the tears just start falling.

437
00:18:52,580 --> 00:18:55,240
I've never cried in front of anyone before.

438
00:18:55,700 --> 00:18:57,580
I really don't understand
what's wrong with me.

439
00:19:04,740 --> 00:19:06,850
Why do the tears keep falling?

440
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:13,320
Ah...

441
00:19:14,310 --> 00:19:15,310
Huh?

442
00:19:16,370 --> 00:19:17,430
Is this...

443
00:19:19,600 --> 00:19:20,600
what it feels like...

444
00:19:23,060 --> 00:19:25,590
to truly fall in love with someone?

445
00:19:41,080 --> 00:19:42,660
Don't ask me.

446
00:19:44,690 --> 00:19:45,890
I see.

447
00:19:47,110 --> 00:19:49,570
Don't cry, Na-chan.

448
00:19:50,080 --> 00:19:52,260
You started crying first.

449
00:19:56,960 --> 00:19:57,960
So-chan.

450
00:19:58,770 --> 00:19:59,770
Yeah?

451
00:20:00,760 --> 00:20:03,540
Isn't it fine if we just
stay the way we are?

452
00:20:04,880 --> 00:20:05,880
Huh?

453
00:20:07,970 --> 00:20:11,860
Even if our relationship
doesn't have a name...

454
00:20:15,990 --> 00:20:19,460
Maybe there isn't a word
to describe it right now,

455
00:20:20,770 --> 00:20:23,480
and it might never even have one.

456
00:20:25,920 --> 00:20:26,920
But...

457
00:20:27,620 --> 00:20:28,790
that's not so bad, right?

458
00:20:32,880 --> 00:20:33,880
Because...

459
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:37,750
we are who we are.

460
00:20:40,180 --> 00:20:40,840
Yeah.

461
00:20:41,090 --> 00:20:42,090
Yeah.

462
00:20:45,540 --> 00:20:47,089
You're way too cute.

463
00:20:47,090 --> 00:20:48,309
Hey!

464
00:20:48,310 --> 00:20:50,120
Take this!

465
00:20:53,990 --> 00:20:55,380
Summer has ended.

466
00:20:55,700 --> 00:20:58,770
So-chan has embarked on his journey.

467
00:20:59,650 --> 00:21:01,830
(1 Week Later)
Everyone's grown up so much.

468
00:21:05,980 --> 00:21:07,420
(To truly fall in love with someone)

469
00:21:07,970 --> 00:21:09,830
This one's good to go.

470
00:21:35,670 --> 00:21:37,139
Time to eat.

471
00:21:37,140 --> 00:21:37,880
Mmhmm.

472
00:21:37,880 --> 00:21:38,640
Basil.

473
00:21:38,640 --> 00:21:39,520
How is it? Is it good?

474
00:21:39,520 --> 00:21:40,180
Yeah.

475
00:21:40,181 --> 00:21:41,239
Natsuki.

476
00:21:41,240 --> 00:21:43,679
I heard your top choice is our university?

477
00:21:43,680 --> 00:21:44,370
Yeah.

478
00:21:44,371 --> 00:21:49,479
Seika University's Faculty of Science would
be a good fit for studying meteorology.

479
00:21:49,480 --> 00:21:50,360
Huh.

480
00:21:50,361 --> 00:21:51,759
I can't believe you want
to study meteorology.

481
00:21:51,760 --> 00:21:53,920
Do you think he was influenced by his dad?

482
00:21:55,490 --> 00:21:56,520
Who knows?

483
00:21:57,510 --> 00:21:59,919
Then you'll have to keep studying hard.

484
00:21:59,920 --> 00:22:00,960
Yeah.

485
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:02,979
Rock.

486
00:22:02,980 --> 00:22:04,370
I'll do my best.

487
00:22:12,150 --> 00:22:15,030
Na-chan.

488
00:22:20,230 --> 00:22:22,690
Do you want to look up at the sky
at the same time today?

489
00:22:27,890 --> 00:22:29,650
No matter how far apart we are,

490
00:22:38,450 --> 00:22:41,670
or how different the clouds
and the color of the sky might be,

491
00:22:45,040 --> 00:22:48,310
we're all connected by the same sky.

492
00:22:57,460 --> 00:23:00,210
I'm going to the UK to see So-chan.

493
00:23:03,290 --> 00:23:06,460
(The story in this
work is purely fictional.)
